2.5 Cleaning and Steaming of 100 L conical vessel.         Date :______________
_______________________________________________________________________________
      Procedure                                |   Time    |Done by |  Ckd. by|
-----------------------------------------------|-----------|--------|---------|
1. Teepol cleaning :                           |           |        |         |
   Prepare 0.5% teepol solution. Add about     |From :_____|        |         |
   15 lts solution to vessel. Bubble with      |           |        |         |
   compressed air for 15 min. and keep stirrer |To   :_____|        |         |
   ON.                                         |           |        |         |

2. Cleaning of vessel to remove teepol : Use   |           |        |         |
   DM water and three rinsing should be given  |           |        |         |
   keep stirrer ON.                            |           |        |         |

3. After ensuring teepol removal, introduce the|From :_____|        |         |
   steam from topside opening.  Steam it for 30|           |        |         |
   min. Open drain valve to remove condensate. |To   :_____|        |         |

4. Stop steaming put distilled water with 1/2" |           |        |         |
   PVC pipe by applying pressure to pressure   |           |        |         |
   vessel.  Rinse inside surface of the vessel |           |        |         |
   by spraying with distilled water.  Use 50   |           |        |         |
   lts. of distilled water.                    |           |        |         |
5. Rinse the vessel with fresh filtered DW just|           |        |         |
   before transfer of bulk solution into the   |           |        |         |
   vessel.                                     |           |        |         |
